    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-4268",
      "problem": "Order the angles of the triangle $\\triangle ABC$ from smallest to largest.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14163584/assets/d4c8a6d27b910f674d8dc85a707e14278fe66dc02c36f4aa75cdc2211cd3bbd2.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The shortest side is $\\overline{BC},$ so the smallest interior angle is $\\angle{A}.$\n\nThe longest side is $\\overline{AB},$ which means that the opposite angle, $\\angle C$, must be the largest one.\n\nTherefore, the required order must be\n\n$$\n\\angle A,\\,  \\angle B,\\,  \\angle C.\n$$",
